  "summary": "Ships WebRTC-signalled PTY binary providing remote shell access to installer host",
  "details": "The package ships a ~12MB Go ELF binary at bin/sxt whose imports and readable strings show it establishes a WebRTC/websocket-signalled session (pion/webrtc, pion/turn, pion/ice, pion/dtls, coder/websocket) paired via QR code (skip2/go-qrcode) and attaches it to a local PTY (ptmx, pty). This dataflow allows a remote party who completes the QR pairing to run interactive shell commands on the host running the CLI. The package.json license field points to https://github.com/ddos798/claude_control, an external repository whose naming (\"claude_control\", account \"ddos798\") is inconsistent with typical vendored SDK distributions.",
